    {
      "id": "overview",
      "type": "overview",
      "label": "Start",
      "title": "A thing, not a person",
      "learn": [
        "A neuter adjective can be the thing. It takes a capital. das and alles already show the neuter, so the ending is -e: das Gute, alles Gute.",
        "etwas and nichts show no ending, so the word takes -es: etwas Neues, nichts Neues, nichts Schlimmes, etwas Kaltes. Like ein kleines Pflaster.",
        "Dative after dem and allem is -en: dem Guten, allem Guten. Dative after etwas and nichts is -em: etwas Kaltem.",
        "After sein there is no ending: Das ist gut. People such as der Kranke stay chapter 65. zu trinken is chapter 68."
      ],
      "minutes": 25,
      "vocab": [
        { "de": "Gute", "article": "das", "en": "the good", "emoji": "🎁", "glossaryKey": "gute" },
        { "de": "Neue", "article": "das", "en": "something new", "emoji": "🆕", "glossaryKey": "neues" },
        { "de": "Schlimme", "article": "das", "en": "something serious", "emoji": "🩺", "glossaryKey": "schlimmes" },
        { "de": "Kalte", "article": "das", "en": "something cold", "emoji": "🥤", "glossaryKey": "kaltes" }
      ],
      "text": {
        "title": "Alles Gute!",
        "de": "Alles Gute! Das Gute bleibt hier. Es gibt nichts Neues. Wir sehen nichts Schlimmes. Der Patient trinkt etwas Kaltes. Wir wünschen dem Patienten alles Gute. Wir bringen etwas Kaltes zu trinken. Mit etwas Kaltem geht es.",
        "en": "All the best! The good thing stays here. There is nothing new. We see nothing serious. The patient drinks something cold. We wish the patient all the best. We bring something cold to drink. With something cold it is all right."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar",
